{"event_type":"review","id":"d8a819465e7cf3479246697e21077c1b43ec1bc8f5d72aa95fd38bb300c5d244","occurred_at":"2026-11-03T17:15:26Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/16b5d457a9cfd5328fc95353884a08de1a3b478d6dc6d500f64303da9dfd9e98","sha256":"16b5d457a9cfd5328fc95353884a08de1a3b478d6dc6d500f64303da9dfd9e98"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/daa28818ce6deea50ae98d211e1d545deb943554c73cd9276f398b93e71db734","sha256":"daa28818ce6deea50ae98d211e1d545deb943554c73cd9276f398b93e71db734"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e466b8ef2df91a0e2c7b4ca96ef6ed7812342605794395e2a79af8547d288d25","sha256":"e466b8ef2df91a0e2c7b4ca96ef6ed7812342605794395e2a79af8547d288d25"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ebeb5f394809b04b3208cb2b38fcd2b4334fc5d71784c0b332719f2463cfe24e","sha256":"ebeb5f394809b04b3208cb2b38fcd2b4334fc5d71784c0b332719f2463cfe24e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3a4f976654f3b219adf48ad3a43f5af01d5ebc2afa15643731ce63e50a33a67b","sha256":"3a4f976654f3b219adf48ad3a43f5af01d5ebc2afa15643731ce63e50a33a67b"}],"attempt_id":"5353c41871690bd167eacb23dee8bbde8327133b7e95f0d3445ff2ab2c59534d:0:1","base":"507340af18150bf950ea6bc0cdeb55efb6168a11","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"a7c1f8f7117fcbcc336e6e9eb4ce92714108ebd9","body":"**Use the reset `previous`, not `retained`, to gate the fresh-outage eligibility check.**\n\nThe eligibility check at Lines 407-427 runs only when `retained === undefined`. Lines 400-405 can reset `previous` to `undefined` while `retained` still holds a completed enrollment. In that case the function skips the check. It does not return `undefined` for a dirty tree, a non-`full` scope, a non-`blocked` completion, or a head, base, or target mismatch. Instead it falls through to a throw:\n\n- If the tree is dirty, Line 437 throws `deferred vendor review requires a committed clean identity`.\n- If the newer `coderabbit` cycle is not `full`, not `clean-tree`, or not `blocked`, `origin` is `undefined` and Line 472 throws.\n- If the newer outage was recorded at another head, `deferVendorReview` throws `origin vendor attempt does not match initial deferral` (`deferredReview.ts:170-178`).\n\nBranches with no lineage admit a fresh review for these states. A branch with a completed lineage throws instead. `prepareDeferredVendorReview` runs before vendor dispatch, so no new `coderabbit` cycle can replace the failing one. The branch then stays blocked until someone edits the ledger by hand.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  if (retained === undefined && vendor?.vendorFailure) {\n+  if (previous === undefined && vendor?.vendorFailure) {\n```\n</details>","id":"5a5f38db2899ea19edc307aaf5ecd9f3751493ef3b24e5ec55f336eda6f6aa96","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/deferredLedger.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use the reset `previous`, not `retained`, to gate the fresh-outage eligibility check."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"6d2c119f9f40168a173474c7ed0fadc923416b2d","body":"**A non-JSON signer reply escapes the `OSError` contract of `publish_ledger` (crq.py:226)**\n\nEvery other failure path in `publish_ledger` raises `OSError`, and the message \"retain publication outbox\" tells callers to treat `OSError` as retain-and-retry. `json.loads(reply)` is different. If the forced command prints a banner, writes partial output, or returns an empty reply, it raises `json.JSONDecodeError`, which is a `ValueError`. A caller that catches only `OSError` then crashes and does not retain the outbox. Map a decode failure to the same `OSError` as a wrong acknowledgement.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if json.loads(reply) != {\"published\": head}:\n+        try:\n+            ack = json.loads(reply)\n+        except ValueError:\n+            ack = None\n+        if ack != {\"published\": head}:\n             raise OSError(\"signer did not acknowledge the exact ledger commit\")\n```\n</details>","id":"c8785e430ce0910a30da36bdc14695f83fc7907f5e4a0dc734ca3ae77f843460","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"A non-JSON signer reply escapes the `OSError` contract of `publishledger` (crq.py:226)"}],"head":"bd2f83593aa7fd5ff632e6b71e27327a76cf3945","head_tree":"e04fe6b46a2a7a3ff99e793e23ea2c0b8de4edf9","input_scope":[{"blob":"6d2c119f9f40168a173474c7ed0fadc923416b2d","intervals":[[11,11],[25,26],[31,31],[34,39],[44,44],[119,161],[177,252],[255,255],[264,267],[269,271],[332,333],[450,488],[490,493],[495,504],[506,506],[524,529],[531,546],[577,653],[755,755],[757,758],[760,760],[786,786],[829,832],[834,842],[849,898],[905,908],[934,937],[947,950],[955,955],[1033,1033],[1090,1091],[1096,1097],[1101,1102],[1114,1634],[1638,1641],[1655,1668],[1685,1685],[1690,1691],[1693,1700],[1705,1705],[1707,1712],[1742,1759],[1763,1763],[1778,1781],[1804,1806],[1815,1815],[1817,1818],[1924,1925],[1930,1946],[1948,1948],[1957,1960],[2050,2086],[2115,2115],[2129,2137],[2141,2141],[2146,2167],[2181,2181],[2208,2209],[2214,2215],[2237,2238],[2244,2244],[2267,2273],[2276,2277],[2307,2307],[2311,2311],[2319,2320],[2328,2328],[2336,2336],[2338,2338],[2347,2347],[2351,2351],[2367,2367],[2377,2377],[2379,2379],[2381,2381],[2387,2393],[2397,2398],[2400,2408],[2416,2416],[2420,2428],[2430,2434],[2437,2438],[2440,2441],[2444,2446],[2449,2449],[2462,2470],[2476,2476],[2480,2480],[2482,2483],[2485,2488],[2496,2735],[2740,2740],[2742,2776],[2778,2779],[2791,2792],[2796,2797],[2808,2810],[2817,2817],[2820,2822],[2831,2831],[2845,2845],[2868,2868],[2873,2873],[2877,2878],[2893,2893],[2952,2954],[2985,2986],[2993,2993],[2997,2997],[3000,3011],[3019,3020],[3026,3026],[3030,3030],[3150,3150],[3165,3169],[3178,3178],[3190,3190],[3192,3198],[3206,3206],[3227,3227],[3244,3244],[3249,3250],[3268,3272]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py"},{"blob":"3fd1a366f75ce150754ecd76ff2fb90efb2a6b25","intervals":[[2,2],[14,14],[19,22],[31,31],[33,33],[35,44],[79,81],[85,88],[92,92],[95,115],[123,127]],"path":"src/ops/dev/disposition.ts"},{"blob":"a7c1f8f7117fcbcc336e6e9eb4ce92714108ebd9","intervals":[[1,944]],"path":"src/ops/dev/internal/deferredLedger.ts"}],"job_id":"5353c41871690bd167eacb23dee8bbde8327133b7e95f0d3445ff2ab2c59534d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"4dc48fb3a076b4576c101aaa3cc8a142ced1a266","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py"},"merge":"ace081cb9cab8fc842a09806d789367f9257d254","method":"pre-merge","pre":"487574e597271f1838a0fc77b58c4b42626e90d4","source_path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py"},"blob":"6d2c119f9f40168a173474c7ed0fadc923416b2d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"e4e15bb8fc0762a9f592d8f3a8eb19b9e886c4eb","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/disposition.ts"},"merge":"ace081cb9cab8fc842a09806d789367f9257d254","method":"pre-merge","pre":"487574e597271f1838a0fc77b58c4b42626e90d4","source_path":"src/ops/dev/disposition.ts"},"blob":"3fd1a366f75ce150754ecd76ff2fb90efb2a6b25","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/disposition.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"ace081cb9cab8fc842a09806d789367f9257d254","method":"pre-merge","pre":"487574e597271f1838a0fc77b58c4b42626e90d4","source_path":"src/ops/dev/internal/deferredLedger.ts"},"blob":"a7c1f8f7117fcbcc336e6e9eb4ce92714108ebd9","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/dev/internal/deferredLedger.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693